WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.334
-Letitia Wright. Thanks so much for coming on.

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:05.767
I'm very -- Everyone is very excited about "Black Panther,"

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:07.100
the sequel.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:08.634
"Black Panther: Wakanda Forever."

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:11.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:14.100
The trailer -- By the way, the trailer got

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:17.934
172 million views in just the first 24 hours.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:19.801
-Yeah. -It, like, broke the Internet.

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:21.434
-Yeah, it did. -It's unbelievable.

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:22.868
I'm so excited about this.

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.701
And you unfortunately got injured

00:00:24.701 --> 00:00:26.167
while you were shooting this film.

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:27.434
-Yes. -And you look okay now.

00:00:27.434 --> 00:00:29.133
Are you doing better? -Yeah.

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:32.467
It was just an unfortunate situation that happened,

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:34.300
but it took me out for, like, three months.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.200
So I went home. I got my mind back together.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.934
I got my healing back together.

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:40.634
And I went back and I finished strong.

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:43.534
So if you want to see how that turned out, November 11th.

00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:46.000
-Yeah! Exactly right. You finished it.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.834
I'm so happy. I'm glad you're better.

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:50.067
-Thank you. -What can we -- What can you

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:52.501
tell us about "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever"?

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:54.067
-Well, firstly I can tell you,

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:57.701
you know, the first movie did so well.

00:00:57.701 --> 00:01:00.133
You know, we made a cultural impact and change.

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:01.801
-You did. -And this film is --

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:05.100
We're trying to follow that -- that same theme,

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.701
you know, of inspiring, you know,

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:09.200
everybody that goes to see it.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.767
We have new cast members,

00:01:10.767 --> 00:01:14.334
such as Dominique Thorne, Michaela Coel.

00:01:14.334 --> 00:01:17.300
So it's jam-packed with lots of adventures.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:20.868
But it -- I feel, for me,

00:01:20.868 --> 00:01:26.701
it's a beautiful contribution to Chadwick's legacy.

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:29.267
I feel like it's a love letter to him.

00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:32.868
I know every day that I went on set, I focused my energy

00:01:32.868 --> 00:01:35.734
on -- on each scene to dedicate it to him.

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:37.934
I wanted to dedicate excellence to this film

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:39.634
so that he could be proud.

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:41.167
-Yeah. Oh, I love that.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:44.400
We loved him. Oh, my goodness.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.334
I cannot wait. I can't wait. -Yes.

00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:49.467
-Do we know who will be the new Black Panther?

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:52.300
-Okay. Yo, Quest, somebody, come get your man.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:53.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:54.868
-No. You can't --

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:56.667
-I am sworn to secrecy. -Of course.

00:01:56.667 --> 00:01:59.033
-By the Marvel spies that are around here somewhere.

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:00.267
-Yeah, they're in the aud--

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:01.634
I just thought maybe you could just give us...

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:02.767
[ Drum roll ]

00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:04.133
No. Okay.

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:05.601
-November 11th. -Alright.

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:07.133
November 11th, we're going to find out.

00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:08.767
I don't want to -- I don't want to get you in trouble.

00:02:08.767 --> 00:02:10.400
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:11.601
Let's talk about your movie, though, "The Silent Twins."

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:14.067
-Yes. -What a great story this is.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.467
-Yeah. -Oh, my gosh.

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:17.567
You're fantastic in it. -Thank you.

00:02:17.567 --> 00:02:19.467
-It's based on a true story. -Mm-hmm.

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:22.067
-How did you hear about this? -I heard about the twins

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:24.267
by watching a documentary years ago.

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:25.868
And I was so intrigued.

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:28.901
And I always wondered if it would ever be made into a film.

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:31.634
Fortunately for me, that became true,

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:33.234
and I got to greenlight the film.

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:35.200
I got to star in it and produce it.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.834
-Look at you. Look at you now.

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:40.067
Come on. Look at you.

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:41.634
-And it's a beautiful story

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:44.367
about twin sisters, June and Jennifer Gibbons.

00:02:44.367 --> 00:02:46.601
They grew up in the '70s in Wales.

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:48.767
Unfortunately, they had a terrible experience

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:52.033
of racial injustice, marginalization,

00:02:52.033 --> 00:02:54.868
and they used silence as a way

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:58.534
to protest against how society made them feel.

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:02.968
And unfortunately, that led to them being placed

00:03:02.968 --> 00:03:05.501
into a psychiatric hospital for 11 years.

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:08.133
And our film -- our film takes a deep dive

00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:10.367
into the wonderful world

00:03:10.367 --> 00:03:13.467
that they created in secrecy to survive.

00:03:13.467 --> 00:03:15.801
It's a rich world of creativity, and I'm so proud of it.

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:17.501
-Because they would talk to each other?

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:18.767
-Yeah, just to each other.

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:20.367
And to everyone else, they were silent.

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:21.801
And they thought it was a mystery,

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:25.501
but our film unlocks a little bit more about why they --

00:03:25.501 --> 00:03:27.167
they were the way they were.

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:29.133
-Ah, it's fascinating. I want to show a clip.

00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:31.400
Here's Letitia Wright in "The Silent Twins."

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:32.567
Take a look at this.

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:33.634
-Jenny!

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:36.033
-Did it arrive? -Yeah!

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:37.968
[ Both chuckle ]

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:44.200
-"The Art of Conversation."

00:03:50.801 --> 00:03:52.133
-How do you open it?

00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:55.234
-Push. And lift.

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:57.901
[ Gasps ]

00:03:57.901 --> 00:04:00.667
-We're writers now. -We're writers now.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:03.033
-Yeah. You're writers now. Come on.

00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:04.767
Letitia Wright, everybody.

00:04:04.767 --> 00:04:07.300
"The Silent Twins" opens in theaters tomorrow.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:09.467
David Blaine joins us after the break.

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:11.467
Stick around, everybody. Come on back.

